# The order matters

I strongly recommend **not** starting with RoboJS.

The dependency order should be approximately:

```text
                 RoboBase
                    │
        ┌───────────┼───────────┐
        ↓           ↓           ↓
    RoboMem    RoboThread    RoboIPC
        │           │           │
        └───────────┼───────────┘
                    ↓
                RoboEvent
                    │
             ┌──────┴──────┐
             ↓             ↓
        RoboGraphics    RoboWindow
             │             │
             └──────┬──────┘
                    ↓
                RoboDOM
                    │
             ┌──────┴──────┐
             ↓             ↓
          RoboHTML      RoboCSS
             │             │
             └──────┬──────┘
                    ↓
                RoboLayout
                    ↓
                RoboPaint
                    ↓
                RoboRender
                    ↓
             RoboCompositor
                    │
                    ↓
                 RoboJS
                    │
                    ↓
                RoboAPI
                    │
                    ↓
                RoboShell
                    │
                    ↓
             Roboticela OS
```

Networking, storage, fonts, security, media, etc. plug into the appropriate places.

### And one more important distinction

If your requirement is **"everything in our runtime must be C"**, then even the names shouldn't necessarily correspond one-to-one with Chromium's internals.

For example, you don't need to create:

```text
RoboBlink
RoboSkia
RoboChromium
RoboMojo
```

Instead, make your own conceptual components:

```text
RoboHTML
RoboCSS
RoboDOM
RoboLayout
RoboPaint
RoboRender
RoboGraphics
RoboIPC
RoboJS
```

That gives Roboticela OS its **own architecture**, rather than Chromium with "Robo" put in front of everything.

